	(footprint "Footprints:Supercap_Radial_D10.0mm_L20.0mm_P5.00mm_Horizontal"
		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "18ec291f-01b8-4140-8a93-3bf7d317c389")
		(at 83.95 129.46 -90)
		(descr "Cylindrical radial EDLC supercapacitor mounted HORIZONTALLY, FOLD-BACK bend: the two radial leads (5.00 mm pitch) exit the end face and fold 180 deg back under the can, so the holes sit ~2.5 mm in FRONT of the face and the can extends over the opposite side of the pads. Can axis parallel to the board, 10.0 mm tall lying on its side. Fold radius ~1.2 mm on the 0.6 mm leads. Drawn for Eaton HV1020-2R7505-R (5.0 F, 2.7 V; ~40 mohm). Pad 1 = POSITIVE. *** DELIBERATELY NO COURTYARD OVER THE BODY *** - the can is glued down and may lie over other components, so the only keep-out is a small courtyard around the two legs, matching the house prismatic-horizontal convention. The body outline is on F.Fab as documentation only and generates no DRC. MECHANICAL: parts under the can must clear its underside (set by your standoff/glue line); parts under the 2.5 mm lead bend must stay low, since the lead descends there from the can's 5.0 mm mid-height to the board. Vertical alternative: stock Capacitor_THT:CP_Radial_D10.0mm_P5.00mm (20 mm standing). Datasheet: Eaton HV series cylindrical cells.")
		(tags "supercapacitor EDLC radial horizontal lay-down bent-lead glued no-keepout tht polarised HV1020")
